      "ok": true,
      "answer": "The search results already returned the full text of those rulebook passages — no additional tool calls are needed. Here is the answer based on the verified tool results:\n\n---\n\n## Long Rests in Frosthaven\n\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, a character may declare a **long rest** instead of selecting two cards to play. This is their entire turn for the round and is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\nTo declare a long rest, the character must have **at least two cards** in their discard pile.\n\nWhen a character long rests, they follow these steps in order:\n\n1. **Lose one card of their choice** from their discard pile and return the remaining cards to their hand. *(Mandatory)*\n2. **Perform *Heal 2*, self.** *(Optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items.** Items can even be used during the same turn in which they are recovered. *(Optional)*\n\n> \"During the Card Selection step, a character may declare a long rest. This constitutes their entire turn for the round, instead of playing two cards, and it is performed on initiative 99.\"\n\n**Source:** Frosthaven Rulebook, p. 38 (passage 125)",
